/E (The Two Heaps coding pattern is a technique used to efficiently solve problems that involve managing two sets of data in a way that allows quick access to the minimum or maximum values from each set. This pattern is often applied to problems dealing with dynamic data streams, such as online algorithms and priority queue-related tasks. The two heaps typically used are the Min Heap and the Max Heap.)
