/E (    3. Iterative Comparison and Merging:          - While the priority queue or heap is not empty:              - Remove the smallest element from the priority                  queue or heap. This element will be the next                  in the merged list.              - Insert the next element from the same list from                  which the smallest element was removed, if                  available.              - Repeat this process until all elements from all lists                  have been merged.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [0]
