/T (The Modified Binary Search is a coding pattern used to optimize certain types of binary search problems. While traditional binary search typically involves searching for a target value in a sorted array by repeatedly dividing the search interval in half, the modified binary search pattern adapts this approach for different scenarios, such as searching in rotated arrays or finding a target sum in sorted arrays.)
